{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 25, :comments ["וַיּוֹרֵהוּ — of the form יוֹרוּ מִשְׁפָּטֶיךָ." "שָׁם שָׂם לוֹ חֹק וּמִשְׁפָּט [וְשָׁם נִסָּהוּ] — There, at Marah, by means of the trial that He placed upon them (to make them thirsty) for water, and afterward healed the water for them, He began to rebuke them so that they would accept upon themselves the statutes and the laws that He would teach them, and He would provide their needs. And how did He set for them a statute and a law? For He said to them: ״אִם שָׁמֹעַ תִּשְׁמַע לְקוֹל ה׳ אֱלֹהֶיךָ״ etc., ״וְשָׁמַרְתָּ כָּל חֻקָּיו״, which He commanded you."], :book :exodus, :voice :rashbam, :lang :en, :chapter 15, :notes {1 "Parenthetical words (הנסיון, להצמיאם) appear in parentheses in the source, likely glosses; translated as integral to the sentence."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:41:42.841662872Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}